Appendable BYTEA Toaster

I. The Pluggable TOAST

On Pluggable TOAST please check contrib/toastapi/README.toastapi

The Appendable BYTEA Toaster is a part of a Pluggable TOAST extension
pack for PostgreSQL.  It is a Toaster for the BYTEA data type that
stores the tail of a TOASTed BYTEA value inline inside the custom
Toast Pointer.  Direct INSERT and UPDATE operations on a BYTEA column
managed by this toaster therefore produce an appendable storage
shape: the next UPDATE that writes a longer value can be served by
extending the inline tail and (when it overflows) by appending new
chunks, without invalidating the existing value_id or rewriting
unchanged chunks.

II. Installation

BYTEA Toaster requires TOAST API (toastapi extension) to be installed.

III. The byteacat ('||') operator

Earlier postgrespro snapshots of bytea_toaster registered a
fast-path implementation of the `||` operator: a custom `append`
function discoverable through `TsrRoutine.get_vtable`, with core
byteacat (src/backend/utils/adt/varlena.c) probing the toaster for
this magic and calling the toaster's append directly when it
matched.

The cleaned toastapi minimization (commit 3ab8a37) removed the
`get_vtable` field from `TsrRoutine`, and the cleaned core's
`byteacat` (src/backend/utils/adt/bytea.c) does not probe for a
custom append.  As a consequence:

  - `bytea_col = bytea_col || new_bytes` UPDATEs now go through
    standard `bytea_catenate` and ordinary tsr_toast/tsr_update.
    The appendable storage shape is still produced, but the
    "patch the inline tail in place" optimisation no longer
    happens on `||`.

  - Direct INSERT and full-value UPDATE through tsr_toast and
    tsr_update continue to exercise the appendable storage path.

  - The previous `bytea_toaster_append` / `bytea_toaster_vtable`
    functions and the `BYTEA_TOASTER_MAGIC` / `ByteaToastRoutine`
    types were unreachable in cleaned and have been removed.

The cleaned line does NOT replace the `||` fast path with a new
Toast API hook.  A bytea-specific operator fast path does not
belong on the general Toast API surface; the Toast API is a
lifecycle interface (toast / detoast / size / delete / copy /
update / validate) and per-type operator fast paths should not
accumulate as Toastapi_*_hook entries.  If appendable bytea is
ever reopened, the right shape is a type-local bytea provider
interface that the bytea type's operators can probe -- a
property of the bytea type, not of the toaster contract.  This
is out of current JBTL scope.
